Generally I would say the game is fun and relaxing to play and for a couple of bucks it's a good value as well. If you're into oldschool games like NES Zelda then this game will probably be up your alley, as it is very reminiscent of that game but with a more modern combat and player attribute system attached to it. Good for a few hours of fun, but the replay value is minimal. Check the blog for full details!

My game crashed on me after five-six hours of building and detailing my park. I was ok with the game crashing, because I thought the autosave had saved a few times at least within the five-six hours, but no. Not a single autosave or backup, the game straight up crashed and none of my files remained, all my work was deleted. Now, normally this wouldn't bother me much, but in a game that is all about dedication and detailing, this is like a slap in the face.
Now generally I do like this game, but it deserves more critique for reasons such as this, and that's what I'm going to give it. A friendly warning to those who, like me, enjoy spending hours and hours, decorating the perfect park;
DON'T TRUST THE AUTOSAVE! Save your game manually every hour or so. Crashes do happen, not only for me.

